# proto-file: intrinsic/world/public/proto/object_world_updates.proto
# proto-message: intrinsic_proto.world.ObjectWorldUpdates

# 3D printer on the ground in front of the reBot, its open front (printer -Y)
# facing the robot (yaw -90 deg about Z), so the spool stack is on the robot's
# left (+Y). The bed centre (printer/bed_frame) lands at x=0.56, y=0,
# z=0.0895; the printer's front edge is at x=0.346. It stood at x=0.36 until
# step 3a, when it moved out 10 cm so the wrist camera sees the whole bed with
# depth, and 10 cm more afterwards for clearance reaching in, which needs a
# flatter grasp (60 deg, configs/rebot/app_config.yaml): at 35 deg the bed's
# far edge is out of reach this far out (offline check).
updates {
  update_transform {
    node_a {
      by_name {
        object {
          object_name: "root"
        }
      }
    }
    node_b {
      by_name {
        object {
          object_name: "printer"
        }
      }
    }
    node_to_update {
      by_name {
        object {
          object_name: "printer"
        }
      }
    }
    a_t_b {
      position {
        x: 0.561
        y: 0.006
        z: 0
      }
      orientation {
        x: 0
        y: 0
        z: -0.70710678
        w: 0.70710678
      }
    }
  }
}
